FINDINGS:
1. [MAJOR] src/repl/shell.rs:221 — join_reader uses handle.join().unwrap_or_default() which silently discards output if the reader thread panics; a panic in read_capped (e.g., OOM during Vec::extend) would return empty output with truncated=false, losing command output without any error indication — VERIFIED: traced line 221 in join_reader where Result from join() is converted to default (Vec::new(), false) on panic
2. [MAJOR] src/repl/mod.rs:2992 — save_session error message "Could not save session: {}" omits the path (destination variable available at line 2985); inconsistent with load_file (line 2768), change_directory (line 2865), export_session (line 3019) which all include paths in errors
3. [MAJOR] src/repl/mod.rs:3047 — restore_session error message "Could not restore session: {}" omits the path (resolved variable available at line 3043); same inconsistency as above
4. [MINOR] src/repl/shell.rs:348 — listing silently skips non-UTF-8 filenames via entry.file_name().to_str().map(...) with continue; on Unix this drops entries with invalid UTF-8 without any indication
5. [MINOR] src/repl/shell.rs:390-458 — resource limit tests (deadline enforcement, output truncation, broken pipe handling) are #[cfg(unix)] only; Windows code paths for 30s deadline, 8MiB cap, 2s drain timeout are untested at unit level
6. [STYLE] src/repl/shell.rs:221 — unwrap_or_default() on thread join Result is a panic-handling anti-pattern; should match on Result and return an error indicating the reader thread failed
